From 8519b60ba484a9a1920724d29bb8a0bbcc01f03d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dardiao <xn--6s1a@outlook.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 12:00:21 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 4/7] local: give the browser a backend url it can actually
 reach

LEMMY_UI_BACKEND is embedded into every rendered page for the *browser* to use, while
LEMMY_UI_BACKEND_INTERNAL is what server-side rendering uses. The compose file only set the
former, to the compose-internal `lemmy:8536`, which no browser can resolve - so every
client-side request (login, voting, posting) failed with "Failed to fetch" while the
server-rendered pages looked fine.

Point the browser-facing url at the proxy on the same origin as the ui, keep the internal one
on the compose network, and add LEMMY_UI_FRONTEND so share links do not point at the internal
`lemmy-ui` hostname either. All three follow LEMMY_UI_PUBLIC_URL, so a real deployment just
sets that to its own address.
---
 docker/README.md          | 12 ++++++++++++
 docker/docker-compose.yml | 14 ++++++++++++--
 2 files changed, 24 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/docker/README.md b/docker/README.md
index fc29f09..71914de 100644
--- a/docker/README.md
+++ b/docker/README.md
@@ -38,6 +38,18 @@ docker compose down            # stop and remove containers (data is kept)
 The web UI is then on <http://localhost:1236>, the API on
 <http://localhost:8536/api/v3/site>, and postgres is published on `5433`.
 
+`lemmy-ui` needs two different backend urls, and they are not interchangeable:
+`LEMMY_UI_BACKEND_INTERNAL` is what server-side rendering uses (over the compose
+network), while `LEMMY_UI_BACKEND` is embedded into the page for the *browser*,
+which cannot resolve compose service names. The compose file points the
+browser-facing one at `localhost:1236` so that it stays on the same origin as the
+UI and goes through the proxy. When the UI is served from somewhere else, pass
+that address instead:
+
+```bash
+LEMMY_UI_PUBLIC_URL=https://niuma.club docker compose up -d
+```
+
 ### Health checks and startup order
 
 Every service defines a `healthcheck`, and `depends_on` uses
diff --git a/docker/docker-compose.yml b/docker/docker-compose.yml
index 13967d3..b4167c2 100644
--- a/docker/docker-compose.yml
+++ b/docker/docker-compose.yml
@@ -77,8 +77,18 @@ services:
       context: ../../lemmy-ui
       dockerfile: dev.dockerfile
     environment:
-      # this needs to match the hostname defined in the lemmy service
-      - LEMMY_UI_BACKEND=lemmy:8536
+      # LEMMY_UI_BACKEND is the url the *browser* uses, so it has to be reachable from the
+      # browser - the compose-internal `lemmy:8536` cannot be resolved there, which made every
+      # client-side request fail with "Failed to fetch" (logins, votes, posting). Point it at
+      # the proxy on the same origin as the ui, then set LEMMY_UI_PUBLIC_URL when the ui is
+      # reached somewhere else, e.g.
+      #   LEMMY_UI_PUBLIC_URL=https://niuma.club docker compose up -d
+      - LEMMY_UI_BACKEND=${LEMMY_UI_PUBLIC_URL:-localhost:1236}
+      # server-side rendering talks to the backend over the compose network
+      - LEMMY_UI_BACKEND_INTERNAL=lemmy:8536
+      # used for share/copy-post links; without it the request host is the internal
+      # `lemmy-ui` hostname behind the proxy
+      - LEMMY_UI_FRONTEND=${LEMMY_UI_PUBLIC_URL:-localhost:1236}
       # set the outside hostname here
       - LEMMY_UI_HTTPS=false
       - LEMMY_UI_ERUDA=true
